    // Game over reasons
    reasonReckless: "You charged after the dragon without any preparation. Your heart was brave, but your body was not ready. The dragon was long gone by the time you realized you had no supplies, no plan, and no hope of catching up. Your spouse was lost to the shadows.",
    reasonDelayedHelp: "You sought the village elder for guidance, but the elder demanded you complete a series of tasks first — tasks that took days. By the time you set out, the dragon's trail had gone cold. The Superlord's fortress remained forever beyond your reach.",
    reasonCave: "The dark cave seemed like a shortcut, but it was a death trap. Goblin warriors lurked in the darkness, and their blades found your throat before you even saw them. Your quest ended in the dark, alone and forgotten.",
    reasonDelayedRiver: "The river path seemed wise, but the mountain streams were swollen from the perpetual storms. You were swept away by a flash flood, your body dashed against the rocks. The dragon flew on, unaware of the hero it had already defeated.",
    reasonTalk: "You tried to reason with the goblins. They laughed — a cruel, mocking sound — and then their spears found your heart. Goblins do not negotiate. Goblins do not show mercy. You should have known better.",
    reasonSteal: "You stole from the market, but the Superlord's spies were everywhere. You were caught, dragged before a magistrate, and thrown into a dark cell. Your quest ended before it truly began, your spouse lost to the darkness.",
    reasonDelayedSneak: "You snuck into the storehouse at night, but the guards were alerted by a loose stone. You were chased from the village, wounded and without supplies. By the time you recovered, the trail was cold and your hope was gone.",
    reasonTraps: "The main path was trapped, just as you feared. A net of enchanted iron rose from the ground, binding you tightly. The guards found you hours later, and your fate was sealed. The mountain claimed another hero.",
    reasonDelayedBridge: "The rope bridge swayed in the wind, but you believed it would hold. It did not. You fell into the chasm, surviving the fall but breaking your leg. You crawled back down the mountain, defeated and alone.",
    reasonFrontdoor: "You stormed the main gate with courage in your heart, but the undead guards were countless. They overwhelmed you, and your sword clattered to the stone floor beside your fallen body. The fortress remained impenetrable.",
    reasonDelayedDistraction: "Your distraction worked — the guards moved away from their posts. But as you slipped inside, a hidden alarm was triggered. You were captured, and the Superlord himself ordered your execution. Your story became a cautionary tale.",
    reasonAttack: "You attacked Malachar directly, but the Superlord's power was beyond your comprehension. With a casual gesture, he hurled you across the throne room. You struck the wall with terrible force, and the world went dark.",
    reasonDelayedDuel: "You challenged Malachar to a duel, and he accepted — but he fought with the skill of a thousand years and the magic of the abyss. Your blade shattered against his dark shield, and your courage was not enough.",
    reasonKill: "You struck down the dragon, believing it to be the greater threat. But as the great beast fell, so too did the cage holding your spouse. The last thing you saw was the life leaving their eyes. Your quest ended in the worst way possible — victorious, yet utterly destroyed.",
    reasonReason: "You tried to speak to the dragon, to reach the creature buried beneath the amulet's control. But the amulet's magic was too strong. The dragon's fire consumed you before you could finish your words. Some chains cannot be broken with words alone.",
    reasonTetrisLost: "You accepted Malachar's challenge, and the duel was his domain. Row after row of dark stone crashed into your grid until there was nowhere left to fall. The Superlord never even rose from his throne. He simply waved a hand, and the darkness took you — your spouse, your hope, and your name all swallowed together.",
    reasonUnknown: "Your journey has ended. The shadows have claimed another hero. But perhaps, in another telling, the story will have a different ending...",

